1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,339
This one line is the most useful sentence anyone's going to say about your mission this week.

2
00:00:06,239 --> 00:00:08,620
It tells me which file and which line,

3
00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:11,786
what's wrong there, and what the game will do about it.

4
00:00:13,586 --> 00:00:15,720
So today you'll learn to read it,

5
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:20,147
and we'll do that by breaking your mission in five places, on purpose.

6
00:00:21,947 --> 00:00:27,014
Lint is a program that reads your files and lists whatever looks wrong,

7
00:00:27,464 --> 00:00:29,342
and it changes nothing at all.

8
00:00:30,242 --> 00:00:31,820
Think of the editor at a publisher:

9
00:00:32,270 --> 00:00:34,380
she reads, and she marks,

10
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:37,026
and you're the one who does the fixing.

11
00:00:38,826 --> 00:00:40,346
The habit has four beats.

12
00:00:41,246 --> 00:00:43,425
You change something, and you save.

13
00:00:43,875 --> 00:00:45,170
Then you run lint on it,

14
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:47,633
and you read the first line it prints.

15
00:00:49,433 --> 00:00:51,422
This is the answer you're hoping for.

16
00:00:52,322 --> 00:00:54,740
There's the file, then the word clean,

17
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:59,623
and then the count line, which says one fact sheet, one story file,

18
00:01:00,073 --> 00:01:02,087
no errors, and no warnings.

19
00:01:03,887 --> 00:01:06,078
Read that count line every time,

20
00:01:06,528 --> 00:01:08,040
even when it says clean.

21
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:11,519
This is the Quest Log,

22
00:01:11,969 --> 00:01:15,391
and Find the Derelict is the first step under First Contact.

23
00:01:16,291 --> 00:01:18,855
In the file, I'm going to misspell one of its fields,

24
00:01:19,305 --> 00:01:21,008
then save, and run lint.

25
00:01:21,908 --> 00:01:23,124
And I get one warning.

26
00:01:24,924 --> 00:01:27,257
Every finding has four parts.

27
00:01:28,157 --> 00:01:30,479
First there's the level, which here is warning.

28
00:01:31,379 --> 00:01:32,997
Then there's the place it's found,

29
00:01:33,447 --> 00:01:35,785
which is line twenty-eight, character one.

30
00:01:36,685 --> 00:01:38,431
Then comes the sentence itself.

31
00:01:39,331 --> 00:01:42,719
And at the very end, in brackets, there's the code,

32
00:01:43,169 --> 00:01:46,851
which is lint's short name for this kind of mistake.

33
00:01:48,651 --> 00:01:51,058
Now read the sentence all the way to the end,

34
00:01:51,508 --> 00:01:53,789
because it tells you three things.

35
00:01:54,689 --> 00:01:59,478
First, what's wrong: Done wen is not a field a quest has.

36
00:02:00,378 --> 00:02:04,797
Next, what the game does about it: nothing reads this line.

37
00:02:05,697 --> 00:02:10,276
And last, what to write instead: did you mean Done when.

38
00:02:12,076 --> 00:02:13,904
So I fix it, I save,

39
00:02:14,354 --> 00:02:16,441
I run lint again, and it's clean.

40
00:02:18,241 --> 00:02:19,956
Now, that was only a warning,

41
00:02:20,406 --> 00:02:22,174
so I could have played this mission.

42
00:02:23,074 --> 00:02:25,268
But with that one word misspelled,

43
00:02:25,718 --> 00:02:27,953
this step can never finish,

44
00:02:28,403 --> 00:02:30,894
and the Quest Log would show it active for the whole game.

45
00:02:31,794 --> 00:02:35,383
A warning can stop your story just as surely as an error.

46
00:02:37,183 --> 00:02:39,435
Every writer does this next one,

47
00:02:39,885 --> 00:02:41,954
and it's to the words in this pane,

48
00:02:42,404 --> 00:02:45,939
the description of Find the Derelict in the Quest Log.

49
00:02:46,839 --> 00:02:48,755
I wrote my line in a word processor,

50
00:02:49,205 --> 00:02:52,050
and it quietly made my quote marks curly.

51
00:02:52,950 --> 00:02:55,022
So now I get three warnings,

52
00:02:55,472 --> 00:02:57,041
one warning for each mark.

53
00:02:58,841 --> 00:03:01,168
All three are on line thirty-one,

54
00:03:01,618 --> 00:03:05,601
and this second number tells me how far along the line to look.

55
00:03:06,501 --> 00:03:07,533
Read to the end again:

56
00:03:07,983 --> 00:03:09,533
the game can't draw this mark,

57
00:03:09,983 --> 00:03:12,771
so it shows the plain one in its place.

58
00:03:13,671 --> 00:03:17,098
So in the Quest Log, the crew would still read my sentence,

59
00:03:17,548 --> 00:03:20,986
with plain quote marks where I typed curly ones.

60
00:03:22,786 --> 00:03:24,514
It's a warning all the same,

61
00:03:24,964 --> 00:03:28,216
because the game only has a plain twin for some characters,

62
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:31,873
and an emoji, for instance, is simply left out.

63
00:03:32,773 --> 00:03:36,040
So I delete each mark and press the plain key,

64
00:03:36,490 --> 00:03:38,235
and lint says it's clean again.

65
00:03:40,035 --> 00:03:43,469
This time I rename a key, on line thirty-three.

66
00:03:44,369 --> 00:03:48,091
Lint complains about line twenty-nine and line thirty-six,

67
00:03:48,541 --> 00:03:51,259
and it says nothing at all about thirty-three.

68
00:03:52,159 --> 00:03:53,470
So why would that be?

69
00:03:55,270 --> 00:03:57,656
Line twenty-nine points at the old key,

70
00:03:58,106 --> 00:04:00,473
and no record has that key any more,

71
00:04:00,923 --> 00:04:02,953
so nothing at all is revealed.

72
00:04:03,853 --> 00:04:06,691
And line thirty-six is the step I renamed.

73
00:04:07,141 --> 00:04:08,740
It's waiting to be revealed,

74
00:04:09,190 --> 00:04:11,125
and now nothing reveals it,

75
00:04:11,575 --> 00:04:14,324
so it would never appear in the Quest Log.

76
00:04:16,124 --> 00:04:18,245
Those are the two ends of one broken link,

77
00:04:18,695 --> 00:04:23,135
and lint names the line that points, and the line that waits.

78
00:04:24,935 --> 00:04:26,537
There's a second way to ask, too.

79
00:04:27,437 --> 00:04:30,104
If I run lint with the word missing on the end,

80
00:04:30,554 --> 00:04:33,933
I get a list of every key I've pointed at and haven't written yet.

81
00:04:34,833 --> 00:04:37,502
While I'm drafting, that's my to-do list.

82
00:04:39,302 --> 00:04:40,581
So I put the key back,

83
00:04:41,031 --> 00:04:43,867
and both warnings go away, and it's clean.

84
00:04:45,667 --> 00:04:47,568
Now it's Derelict Hull's turn,

85
00:04:48,018 --> 00:04:50,993
the hull reading on Science, on the hulk's scan tab.

86
00:04:51,893 --> 00:04:53,363
I delete just one line,

87
00:04:53,813 --> 00:04:55,964
the three hyphens that close this fence.

88
00:04:56,864 --> 00:04:58,503
And that gets me my first error.

89
00:05:00,303 --> 00:05:02,104
The line I deleted was fifty-one,

90
00:05:02,554 --> 00:05:04,541
but lint names line forty-eight.

91
00:05:05,441 --> 00:05:07,897
That's the line where the fence opens,

92
00:05:08,347 --> 00:05:10,163
the fence that now never closes.

93
00:05:11,063 --> 00:05:12,982
And the sentence tells me the rest:

94
00:05:13,432 --> 00:05:16,482
the lines under the fields were read as fields,

95
00:05:16,932 --> 00:05:18,885
so this record has no text.

96
00:05:19,785 --> 00:05:23,171
In the game, Science can never finish scanning the hulk:

97
00:05:23,621 --> 00:05:27,887
its Scan button just keeps saying Queue Scan,

98
00:05:28,337 --> 00:05:30,159
and the hulk stays unknown.

99
00:05:31,059 --> 00:05:32,932
It gives me the fix as well,

100
00:05:33,382 --> 00:05:36,510
which is to add a line of three hyphens under the last field.

101
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:40,337
So I type it back, and it's clean.

102
00:05:41,237 --> 00:05:43,843
It's the same lesson as the last break:

103
00:05:44,293 --> 00:05:47,750
the line lint names isn't always the line I changed,

104
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,801
so let the sentence tell you where to look.

105
00:05:52,601 --> 00:05:54,653
The hashes say where a record sits.

106
00:05:55,553 --> 00:05:58,047
So let's give this one a hash too many,

107
00:05:58,497 --> 00:06:00,383
and that gives me one error.

108
00:06:01,283 --> 00:06:03,768
This heading now has four hashes,

109
00:06:04,218 --> 00:06:06,448
and the one it sits under has two.

110
00:06:07,348 --> 00:06:09,262
And look at what the game does about it:

111
00:06:09,712 --> 00:06:12,947
it reads the heading as if it had three.

112
00:06:13,847 --> 00:06:15,933
Here that guess happens to be right,

113
00:06:16,383 --> 00:06:18,647
so nothing at all is lost.

114
00:06:20,447 --> 00:06:23,454
In break one, a warning stopped my story,

115
00:06:23,904 --> 00:06:26,601
and here an error costs me nothing.

116
00:06:27,501 --> 00:06:30,714
So I don't judge a finding by its level.

117
00:06:31,164 --> 00:06:33,660
I read its sentence instead.

118
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:37,300
I take the extra hash off,

119
00:06:37,750 --> 00:06:40,673
and now let's go the other way, down to one hash.

120
00:06:41,573 --> 00:06:44,656
And that gives me six findings.

121
00:06:46,456 --> 00:06:48,429
This is the point where people give up,

122
00:06:48,879 --> 00:06:51,017
so here's the rule to follow:

123
00:06:51,467 --> 00:06:53,046
read the first one only.

124
00:06:53,946 --> 00:06:57,231
It's about line forty-seven, the line I changed,

125
00:06:57,681 --> 00:07:02,575
and it says one hash starts a new title, so give it three.

126
00:07:03,475 --> 00:07:06,268
The others are about two records further down,

127
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:08,401
records that I never touched,

128
00:07:08,851 --> 00:07:11,296
and their advice would actually make things worse.

129
00:07:13,096 --> 00:07:14,883
So I put the hashes back,

130
00:07:15,333 --> 00:07:17,712
and all six go at once.

131
00:07:18,612 --> 00:07:21,606
Fix the first finding, and then run lint again.

132
00:07:23,406 --> 00:07:24,499
Now for the honest part.

133
00:07:25,399 --> 00:07:26,931
I leave myself a note,

134
00:07:27,381 --> 00:07:31,343
the way I would in a manuscript, with a hash in front of it.

135
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:33,723
And lint still says clean.

136
00:07:34,623 --> 00:07:40,156
But in the game, in the Quest Log's pane, my note is part of the description the crew reads.

137
00:07:41,956 --> 00:07:44,635
In this file, a note starts with two slashes.

138
00:07:46,435 --> 00:07:50,620
Clean means every shape is one that lint knows,

139
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:53,257
every key that's pointed at exists,

140
00:07:53,707 --> 00:07:55,334
and the story file can be read.

141
00:07:56,234 --> 00:07:58,557
It doesn't mean the mission does what I meant it to.

142
00:07:59,457 --> 00:08:02,159
The page has a short list of the things lint can't see.

143
00:08:03,959 --> 00:08:06,563
Lint reads every one of your files,

144
00:08:07,013 --> 00:08:08,332
but it doesn't run them.

145
00:08:09,232 --> 00:08:11,609
So the second check is to play for a minute,

146
00:08:12,059 --> 00:08:14,118
and then read the logs.

147
00:08:15,918 --> 00:08:19,105
Here's that extra hash again, this time in the game.

148
00:08:20,005 --> 00:08:22,870
This is Science, with the hulk's scan tab open,

149
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,858
and the hull reading is still there,

150
00:08:25,308 --> 00:08:27,452
because the game took the hash off for me.

151
00:08:28,352 --> 00:08:29,951
And here's the runtime log:

152
00:08:30,401 --> 00:08:33,875
one line, with the line number and the fix.

153
00:08:34,775 --> 00:08:37,598
That's exactly what lint told me before I played,

154
00:08:38,048 --> 00:08:39,815
which is why lint comes first.

155
00:08:41,615 --> 00:08:43,831
So I fix it, and lint says clean.

156
00:08:44,731 --> 00:08:46,762
But the log still has its line in it,

157
00:08:47,212 --> 00:08:49,147
because lint leaves the logs alone.

158
00:08:50,047 --> 00:08:51,958
They're the game's notes on my last play.

159
00:08:53,758 --> 00:08:55,119
So I play the mission again,

160
00:08:55,569 --> 00:08:58,664
and there's the hull reading on Science, just as it should be.

161
00:08:59,564 --> 00:09:01,606
This time both logs are empty,

162
00:09:02,056 --> 00:09:04,576
and that's what you want to see after every play.

163
00:09:06,376 --> 00:09:08,212
Now use it on your own words.

164
00:09:09,112 --> 00:09:12,534
Rewrite the three descriptions, and the three readings,

165
00:09:12,984 --> 00:09:17,028
and after every one of them, save, run lint, and read the count line.

166
00:09:17,928 --> 00:09:20,430
Then play the mission, and read both logs.

167
00:09:22,230 --> 00:09:26,506
Next time, we'll put names to two words you saw in this file today:

168
00:09:26,956 --> 00:09:28,584
a role, and a signal.
